2. BINARY SEARCH TREE (BST) INSERTION TRACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sequence inserted: 50, 30, 70, 20, 40, 60, 80[cite: 79]

- Insert 50: Tree is empty -> becomes root[cite: 79].
- Insert 30: 30 < 50 -> attached to the left of 50[cite: 79].
- Insert 70: 70 > 50 -> attached to the right of 50[cite: 79].
- Insert 20: 20 < 50 (go left), 20 < 30 (attached to the left of 30)[cite: 79].
- Insert 40: 40 < 50 (go left), 40 > 30 (attached to the right of 30)[cite: 79].
- Insert 60: 60 > 50 (go right), 60 < 70 (attached to the left of 70)[cite: 79].
- Insert 80: 80 > 50 (go right), 80 > 70 (attached to the right of 70)[cite: 79].

