3. MAX-HEAP TRACE (Insertion and Deletion / Extract-Max)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A) Insertion Trace: Insert 10 into Max-Heap [9, 7, 8, 3, 2, 5][cite: 88]
- Step 1: Append 10 at the next open slot (index 6) to keep the tree complete[cite: 88].
- Step 2: Compare 10 with its parent at index 2 (value 8); 10 > 8, so swap[cite: 88].
- Step 3: Compare 10 with its new parent at index 0 (value 9); 10 > 9, so swap again[cite: 88].
- Step 4: 10 reaches the root (no higher parent); heap property restored[cite: 88].
Final Max-Heap Array: [10, 7, 9, 3, 2, 5, 8][cite: 88]

B) Deletion Trace (Extract-Max): Remove max from [10, 7, 9, 3, 2, 5, 8][cite: 89]
- Step 1: Root (10) is removed and reported as the maximum[cite: 89].
- Step 2: Move the last element (8) into the root, and shrink the array by one[cite: 89].
- Step 3: Compare 8 with its larger child (9); 9 > 8, so swap[cite: 89].
- Step 4: 8 (at index 2) has child 5; 5 < 8, so stop; heap property restored[cite: 89].
Final Max-Heap Array: [9, 7, 8, 3, 2, 5][cite: 89]
